<title>USA: Conrail reaches labor pact with dispatchers.</title>
<headline>Conrail reaches labor pact with dispatchers.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Conrail Inc and the System Committee of the American Train Dispatchers Department of the Brotherhood of Locomotive Engineers Tuesday said they reached a tentative agreement on a new labor contract.</p>
<p>The agreement covers all outstanding issues between the parties, including wages, health and welfare benefits and work rules.</p>
<p>Details of the agreement are being withheld pending membership ratification.</p>
<p>The ATDD/BLE represents approximately 400 train dispatchers on Conrail.</p>
<p>With this ATDD/BLE agreement, Conrail has now reached agreement with unions representing 87 percent of its employees subject to collective bargaining.</p>
</text>
